        # So if x is contained in self._iv[i], we have self._iv[i][0] == x (since start >= x and we need s <= x).
        # But wait, what if x is inside an earlier interval? For example, intervals = [(1, 5)], x = 3.
        # bisect_left with (3,) on [(1,5)]: since (1,5) < (3,), it returns 0. Then we check self._iv[0][0] <= 3 < self._iv[0][1], which is 1 <= 3 < 5, True.
